-- title:
--   Marked lift with Legendre cross vanishing only at T=0
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a local integral domain of characteristic $0$, $k$ an algebraically closed field, and $\pi\colon\mathcal O\to k$ a surjective ring homomorphism such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\ker\pi)$-adically complete; assume $2\neq 0$ in $k$. Let $W$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$, let $n$ be a natural number with $2n+1\neq 0$ in $k$ and $2n+1$ not a square in $\mathbb N$, let $Q_0$ be a point of $W$ of exact additive order $2n+1$, and let $\gamma_0$ be a Weierstrass variable change with $\gamma_0\cdot W=W.\mathrm{veluQuotient}(S_0)$, where $S_0$ is the finite set of coordinate pairs of the points $kQ_0$ for $1\le k\le n$ (the point at infinity being recorded as $(0,0)$) and $\mathrm{veluQuotient}$ replaces $a_4$ by $a_4-5\sum_{P\in S_0}t_P$ and $a_6$ by $a_6-b_2\sum_{P\in S_0}t_P-7\sum_{P\in S_0}w_P$. Finally let $(x_1,y_1)$ and $(x_2,y_2)$ be nonsingular affine points of $W$ annihilated by $2$, with $x_1\neq x_2$. The conclusion asserts the existence of: an elliptic Weierstrass curve $E$ over $\mathcal O[[T]]$ whose image under $\pi\circ(\text{constant coefficient})$ is exactly $W$ and whose $j$-invariant has non-constant reduction $\mathrm{map}\,\pi\,(j_E)\in k[[T]]$; a monic $h\in\mathcal O[[T]][X]$ dividing $E.\mathrm{pre}\Psi'_{2n+1}$ whose reduction is $\prod_{P\in S_0}(X-P_1)$, such that the Kohel quotient $E.\mathrm{kohelQuotient}\,h$ — the curve $\mathrm{veluQuotientOfSums}$ of $E$ for $t=6p_2+b_2p_1+(\deg h)b_4$ and $w=10p_3+2b_2p_2+3b_4p_1+(\deg h)b_6$, with $p_i$ the power sums of the roots of $h$ — is again elliptic; and power series $e_1,e_2,e'_1,e'_2\in\mathcal O[[T]]$ with $\Psi_2^{\,2}$ of $E$ vanishing at $e_1$ and $e_2$, $\Psi_2^{\,2}$ of the Kohel quotient vanishing at $e'_1$ and $e'_2$, whose constant terms reduce under $\pi$ to $x_1$, $x_2$, $u_0^{-2}(x_1-r_0)$ and $u_0^{-2}(x_2-r_0)$ respectively, and such that the cross expression $(-b_2(E)-8e_1-4e_2)(e'_2-e'_1)-(-b_2(E.\mathrm{kohelQuotient}\,h)-8e'_1-4e'_2)(e_2-e_1)$ has constant term mapping to $0$ under $\pi$ while its coefficientwise reduction along $\pi$ is a nonzero element of $k[[T]]$.
--
--   This is the deformation-theoretic half of Deuring's lifting theorem in residue characteristic different from $2$: the curve $W$, isomorphic to its quotient by the cyclic group generated by $Q_0$, is deformed non-isotrivially over the formal disc together with a lift of that cyclic subgroup (a monic factor of the $(2n+1)$-division polynomial) and with lifts of two $2$-torsion $x$-coordinates on the curve and on its quotient, the comparison of Legendre moduli being arranged to degenerate only at the closed point. It is used in the passage to a valuation subring in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_valuationSubring_lift_variableChange_veluQuotient_apply_twoTorsion_eq_of_smul_eq_veluQuotient`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_valuationSubring_lift_variableChange_veluQuotient_apply_twoTorsion_eq_of_smul_eq_veluQuotient).
